					p#action-plan-instructions.source-note
						strong How to use this table:
						|  Leave an action unticked while it is outstanding. Tick its “Complete” box only when the required evidence is held, then enter the actual completion date.
					.table-scroll(tabindex="0", aria-label="Scrollable table: 5. Pre-issue action plan")
						table
							caption 5. Pre-issue action plan
							thead
								tr
									th(scope="col") ID
									th(scope="col") Pri.
									th(scope="col") Action / evidence
									th(scope="col") Owner
									th(scope="col") Done / date
							tbody
								+actionRow("A1", "A", "Confirm the 10 × 11 metre Royal Society tent footprint, PhotoSYNTH’s 5 × 11 metre allocation, usable internal dimensions, exact location, public capacity, opening hours and accessible route/threshold. Record Pink Gate as the access point and toolkit.redefined.confusion as the site What3Words reference.", "Team Lead")
								+actionRow("A2", "A", "Obtain the festival emergency procedures from the Site/Production Office and confirm Event Control, alarm, exits/assembly, fire point, security, severe weather and radio arrangements. Record channel 2 for build/break medical incidents and channel 1 for show-day Event Control.", "Team Lead")
								+actionRow("A3", "A", "Obtain tent handover/certification, engineering drawings/calculations, anchorage/ballast plan, flame-retardancy evidence, permitted attachments, occupancy, wind limits and adverse-weather plan. Confirm the structural-engineer inspection on the Tuesday and Local Authority inspection on the Wednesday before the event; resolve whether PhotoSYNTH equipment must be installed before those sign-offs.", "Tent supplier")
								+actionRow("A4", "A", "Submit power requirements in advance; approve the electrical schedule and temporary supply; retain installation verification and equipment inspection/testing evidence. Festival power must not connect non-compliant equipment.", "Electrical competent person")
								+actionRow("A5", "A", "Approve final layout showing exits, clear route, wheelchair turning space, queue, cable routes, speakers, charging and storage.", "Technical & Privacy Lead + Access & Safeguarding Lead")
								+actionRow("A6", "A", "Set/test maximum sound level and speaker separation; document quiet/headphone option and alarm audibility.", "Technical & Privacy Lead")
								+actionRow("A7", "A", "Verify visual effects and disable hazardous flashing; prepare photosensitivity warning and immediate stop/blackout control.", "Technical & Privacy Lead")
								+actionRow("A8", "A", "Verify and document that the deployed PhotoSYNTH build processes camera frames in real time entirely on device and stores or transmits no video footage. Publish a short, accessible participant notice stating this clearly; identify the controller, purpose and lawful basis for any transient processing; record the software/configuration checked; and keep participant agreement separate from the UK GDPR lawful basis.", "Technical & Privacy Lead + data controller")
								+actionRow("A9", "A", "Assign the four combined team roles and Team Lead deputy; finalise rota, breaks, competence/DBS requirements and staff briefing record.", "Team Lead")
								+actionRow("A10", "A", "Complete pre-opening inspection and table-top emergency walk-through with all on-duty staff.", "Team Lead")
