					article.risk-card#r01(data-risk="r01 — coordination, competence and uncontrolled change")
						h3 R01 — Coordination, competence and uncontrolled change
						.table-scroll(tabindex="0", aria-label="Scrollable table: R01 — Coordination, competence and uncontrolled change")
							table
								caption R01 — Coordination, competence and uncontrolled change
								thead
									tr
										th(scope="col") Phase
										th(scope="col") People affected
										th(scope="col") Initial L
										th(scope="col") S
										th(scope="col") R
										th(scope="col") Residual L
										th(scope="col") S
										th(scope="col") R
								tbody
									tr
										td All phases
										td Staff, contractors, visitors
										td 3
										td 4
										td.score-high 12
										td 1
										td 4
										td.score-low 4
						p
							strong Potential harm: 
							| Conflicting instructions, missed controls, unsafe improvisation or delayed emergency response.
						h4 Required controls
						ul
							li Appoint the Team Lead and named deputy for every shift; both must understand this assessment and the festival Event Safety Plan.
							li Every worker must complete the site safety induction and hold the confirmation email, accreditation and Site Office authorisation before access. Record attendance and brief role boundaries, stop-work authority, welfare, first aid, emergency signals and site rules.
							li Nominate the event-cover person in charge; ensure the Site Office has crew mobile numbers and a 24-hour contractor emergency number; collect the arranged radio/channel list and keep the radio active while responsible for cover.
							li Agree in writing the division of responsibility between designerzen/PhotoSYNTH, the Royal Society as host programme/tent, the tent/production supplier and Camp Bestival, including staffing, infrastructure, public operation, emergency interfaces and approval authority.
							li Each employer appoints competent assistance and consults affected workers or their representatives on this assessment, new equipment/technology, training and material changes; record comments and resulting decisions before issue.
							li Confirm whether workers include under-18s, agency/temporary staff, disabled workers, volunteers, lone workers, or notified pregnant workers/new mothers and complete the additional or individual assessment, information, supervision and reasonable adjustments their circumstances require.
							li Use the opening checklist at the start of every operating day and after material change, severe weather, equipment replacement or an incident.
							li Record new hazards using the dynamic assessment log. Stop the affected activity where the risk cannot immediately be controlled.
						p.risk-owner
							strong Owner / verification: 
							| Team Lead before access to site; daily briefing record and dynamic log.
					article.risk-card#r02(data-risk="r02 — vehicle movements during load-in and load-out")
						h3 R02 — Vehicle movements during load-in and load-out
						.table-scroll(tabindex="0", aria-label="Scrollable table: R02 — Vehicle movements during load-in and load-out")
							table
								caption R02 — Vehicle movements during load-in and load-out
								thead
									tr
										th(scope="col") Phase
										th(scope="col") People affected
										th(scope="col") Initial L
										th(scope="col") S
										th(scope="col") R
										th(scope="col") Residual L
										th(scope="col") S
										th(scope="col") R
								tbody
									tr
										td Set-up / break
										td Crew, contractors, pedestrians
										td 3
										td 5
										td.score-very-high 15
										td 1
										td 5
										td.score-moderate 5
						p
							strong Potential harm: 
							| Collision, crushing, trapping or fatal injury where vehicles and people share routes.
						h4 Required controls
						ul
							li Enter through Pink Gate on the B3070 and follow event road signs, not Sat Nav. Vehicles must not pass through Wool, Coombe Keynes or East Lulworth; this is a licence condition.
							li Observe the site’s 08:00–20:00 access/working hours and 08:00–18:30 delivery window. On show days there is no on-site traffic movement after 08:00 until Event Control lifts the curfew by radio.
							li Follow the 10 mph site limit and steward instructions. The site is Hazz-Off: do not use hazard lights while moving; use flashing beacons or headlights as directed.
							li Keep vehicles and plant on hard standing, hardcore tracks or Trakway. Do not drive on grass without Site Management permission and never block the site’s one-road-in/one-road-out route.
							li Complete loading activities before public admission wherever practicable and maintain physical separation between pedestrians and vehicles.
							li Use a trained banksman for reversing or restricted visibility; nobody stands behind or between a moving vehicle and a fixed object.
							li Secure loads in transit; open doors carefully and unload only on hard standing/Trakway into a stable, segregated area. A named team member must be present to receive each delivery; arrange collection before the contractor leaves site.
							li Wear high-visibility clothing and protective safety boots throughout build/break; keep emergency vehicle routes clear.
						p.risk-owner
							strong Owner / verification: 
							| Operations & Logistics Lead / festival traffic team at each vehicle movement.
