							li Visually inspect plugs, cables, enclosures and strain relief before each day; quarantine, label and remove damaged, wet, overheated or unreliable equipment.
							li Use outdoor-rated connectors/enclosures where exposed; keep connections raised, protected from weather and away from public access. Never daisy-chain extension leads or overload outlets.
							li Route and protect cables without obstructing exits. Keep drinks away from electrical equipment and isolate power before cleaning, repositioning or responding to water ingress.
							li Before use, staff explain the safe operation of electronic and musical equipment, including controlled volume, safe handling and the immediate stop control; supervise participants throughout.
							li Know the accessible emergency isolation point. Only the competent electrician may modify or repair the temporary installation.
