						p
							strong Potential harm: 
							| Distress, loss of trust, safeguarding concern or conflict if participants believe they are being recorded, identified or monitored beyond the live interaction.
						h4 Required controls
						ul
							li Display a short, clear and accessible notice before use: the camera analyses facial movement and expressions in real time entirely on the PhotoSYNTH device; no video footage is recorded, stored or transmitted.
							li The Technical & Privacy Lead must verify the deployed software and configuration before opening and after any change, and retain a simple data-flow/configuration record showing local real-time processing, no video storage and no video transmission.
							li The identified data controller must document the limited purpose and lawful basis for any transient personal-data processing and provide accessible information before the camera is activated. Screen for a DPIA and obtain specialist advice if the processing or deployment changes in a way likely to create high risk.
							li Do not enable recording, image capture, cloud/remote inference, video telemetry, video transmission or retention. Treat any proposal or unexpected indication of those functions as a material change: stop camera operation and complete technical, privacy and safeguarding review before restart.
							li Obtain informed agreement before activating the camera and provide a meaningful non-camera demonstration or opt-out where practicable.
							li Record that participant agreement to take part is not, by itself, the documented UK GDPR lawful basis.
							li Do not photograph or record participants on separate devices without explicit consent under the event/media policy; apply additional safeguards for children and adults at risk.
							li Aim the camera only at the intended interaction zone and prevent unintended capture of passers-by where practicable.
							li Stop immediately if a person withdraws consent or appears distressed; direct privacy complaints or data incidents to the named data/privacy contact.
						p.risk-owner
							strong Owner / verification: 
							| Technical & Privacy Lead verifies the deployed on-device configuration, maintains the participant notice and confirms the absence of video storage/transmission; the data controller confirms the proportionate assessment and lawful-basis record; all team members obtain participant agreement and enforce the opt-out.
