						h4 Required controls
						ul
							li Provide hand-cleaning facilities and clean shared touch points, headphones and instruments with manufacturer-compatible products at a defined frequency and when visibly contaminated.
							li Use detergents, soap, bleach and other cleaning agents only at festival-designated points. Never use drinking-water standpipes for washing equipment or personal hygiene; contain resulting grey water as directed.
							li Do not share items that cannot be hygienically cleaned between users where there is contact with the face, mouth or broken skin; use replaceable covers where suitable.
							li Because members of the team include disabled artists who remain vulnerable to COVID-19, each team member takes a lateral-flow test before travelling to site where tests are available. Anyone with a positive result, a high temperature or symptoms that make them unfit for work must not attend and must notify the Team Lead.
							li Testing supplements rather than replaces ventilation, hygiene, staying away when infectious and current public-health advice; maintain contingency staffing for absence.
							li Maximise tent ventilation without compromising structural/weather safety and avoid unnecessary crowd density.
							li Agree individual adjustments for clinically vulnerable staff, such as lower-contact duties, enhanced ventilation, masks or shorter shifts, without stigma.
